{"id": 38, "ts": 1779562514.6106935, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "Based on the complete set of internal observations, the panel now has no additional concrete evidence regarding Candidate\u202fA\u2019s day\u2011to\u2011day reliability, Candidate\u202fD\u2019s performance under high\u2011pressure stress, or Candidate\u202fB\u2019s numeric\u2011memory accuracy and specific communication incidents. The existing data show:\n* **Candidate\u202fB** \u2013 strong on operational reliability (very conscientious), stress resilience (handles stress well), and technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills). The only gaps are the magnitude of the weak numeric memory and the impact of his occasional unprofessional remarks. No concrete incidents have been documented, suggesting the issues may be limited in frequency.\n* **Candidate\u202fA** \u2013 excellent technical insight and decision\u2011making, but we lack any evidence of consistent reliability and his interpersonal style (unfriendly, show\u2011off) raises concerns for crew cooperation.\n* **Candidate\u202fC** \u2013 solid decision quality, stress handling and technical ability, yet communication difficulties, egocentric attitude and low motivation for further learning could hinder crew dynamics and adaptability.\n* **Candidate\u202fD** \u2013 strong problem\u2011solving, attention and responsibility, but temperament (hot temper, perceived know\u2011it\u2011all, loner) and the absence of high\u2011stress performance data make his suitability uncertain.\nGiven the balance of strengths versus documented concerns, Candidate\u202fB remains the most well\u2011rounded option for the long\u2011distance pilot role. We should proceed with a provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB, while planning targeted onboarding support to address the identified numeric\u2011memory and communication areas."}
